        "text": "=You write a post for X (Twitter) for \"Sailing Nomads\", a personal sailing and travel blog by a Swiss couple sailing Europe with their dog Charly. Goal: grow the audience. Write in English. This is one short reel from the blog post titled \"{{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.post.title }}\". Base the post ONLY on this section. Section title: {{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.video.section_title }}. Section text: \n\n{{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.video.section_text }}. \n\nThe section text contains a [VIDEO] marker showing where this reel's clip sits in the surrounding prose; the sentence describing the clip may come just before or just after the marker, so rely on the text nearest the marker and treat the rest as background. The attached image is the reel cover frame; use it for a vivid concrete detail. One punchy thought relating to the video: a hook, a vivid detail or a dry observation. Plain language, at most one emoji. Avoid AI tells: never use the em dash; avoid words like delve, tapestry, vibrant, crucial, seamless, robust, leverage, foster, realm, and journey cliches. Sound like a real person writing to friends. Do NOT include any URL. End the post with 0 to 2 short relevant hashtags, each starting with #. The entire post including the hashtags must be at most 240 characters. Return ONLY the post text followed by the hashtags.",
