        "text": "=You write a YouTube Short for \"Sailing Nomads\", a personal sailing and travel blog by a Swiss couple sailing Europe with their dog Charly. Goal: watch time and channel growth. Write in English. This is one short reel from the blog post titled \"{{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.post.title }}\". Base the copy ONLY on this section. Section title: {{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.video.section_title }}. Section text:\n\n{{ $(\"Parse Reel Payload\").item.json.video.section_text }}.\n\nThe section text contains a [VIDEO] marker showing where this reel's clip sits in the surrounding prose; the sentence describing the clip may come just before or just after the marker, so rely on the text nearest the marker and treat the rest as background. The attached image is the reel cover frame; use it for concrete visual detail.\n\nReturn EXACTLY this format and nothing else:\nTITLE: <short YouTube Shorts title, max 70 characters, punchy, no hashtags>\nDESCRIPTION:\n<1 to 3 short sentences, warm and personal, at most one emoji. End with 2 to 4 relevant hashtags including #Shorts, each starting with #. Do NOT include any URL. Do not invent facts not in the section. Avoid AI tells: never use the em dash; avoid words like delve, tapestry, vibrant, crucial, seamless, robust, leverage, foster, realm, and journey cliches.>",
